{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 1. Prerequisites and Foundation Knowledge\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 1.1 What You Need to Know Before Starting\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Before diving into creating camera nodes, you need to understand fundamental ROS 2 concepts. This section builds the foundation for everything that follows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 What is a ROS 2 Node?\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A node is a process that performs computation. Think of it as a small program that does one specific job. Instead of building one monolithic program, ROS 2 encourages you to build many small, focused nodes that communicate with each other.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Traditional Approach:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab One big program does everything\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Reads camera, processes images, controls motors\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hard to debug, hard to reuse\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ROS 2 Approach:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Camera Node - only handles camera\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Image Processor Node - only processes images\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Motor Controller Node - only controls motors\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Each can be tested, debugged, and reused independently\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ROS 2 Communication: Topics\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Nodes communicate by publishing and subscribing to topics. A topic is like a radio channel - one node broadcasts (publishes) on the channel, and other nodes listen (subscribe) to it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Publisher Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 self.publisher = self.create_publisher(Image, 'camera/image', 10)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 self.publisher.publish(image_msg)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Subscriber Example:}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 self.subscription = self.create_subscription(\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Image, 'camera/image', self.callback, 10)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The number 10 is the queue size - how many messages to buffer if the subscriber is slow.\par}
